  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and comparing the variances of the lotteries and selecting the one with higher variance. The individual does not compute or refer to variance, nor do they mention any concept related to statistical spread or dispersion. Instead, they focus on the trade-off between loss amount and loss probability, reasoning about whether the probability difference justifies the larger loss. Their justification is consistent with a form of expected utility or intuitive cost-benefit trade-off, not variance maximization. There is no indication that the individual considered the information relevant to the decision reason (variance), nor did they apply the rule of preferring higher variance. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
