  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on comparing the variances of the two lotteries and preferring the one with the larger variance. Variance can be computed from the outcomes and probabilities. For Lottery A: outcome -3000 with probability 0.002, and 0 with probability 0.998. For Lottery B: outcome -6000 with probability 0.001, and 0 with probability 0.999. The expected value of A is (-3000)(0.002) + (0)(0.998) = -6. The variance of A is E[X²] - (E[X])² = [(-3000)² * 0.002 + 0] - (-6)² = (9,000,000 * 0.002) - 36 = 18,000 - 36 = 17,964. For Lottery B: expected value is (-6000)(0.001) = -6. E[X²] = (36,000,000 * 0.001) = 36,000. Variance = 36,000 - (-6)² = 36,000 - 36 = 35,964. Thus, Lottery B has a higher variance (35,964 > 17,964), so the decision reason would prefer Lottery B. The reason is applicable to the decision problem.",
